@@ -137,6 +137,59 @@ to indicates which is the bigger version:
 * ``1`` if the first version is greater than the second version.
 
 
+pysemver sort
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Sort versions, oldest first.
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+   pysemver sort [<VERSION>...]
+
+.. option:: <VERSION>
+
+    Versions to sort. If none are given, versions are read from
+    *standard in*, one per line; blank lines are ignored.
+
+The sorted versions are printed on *standard out* as plain text,
+one version per line, which makes the output easy to process with
+a ``while read`` loop::
+
+    $ pysemver sort 1.10.0 1.2.0 1.2.0-rc.1
+    1.2.0-rc.1
+    1.2.0
+    1.10.0
+
+If any version is not a valid version, nothing is printed on standard
+out and the command fails with return code 2.
+
+
+pysemver latest
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Print the highest version that is not a prerelease.
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+   pysemver latest [<VERSION>...]
+
+.. option:: <VERSION>
+
+    Versions to search. If none are given, versions are read from
+    *standard in*, one per line; blank lines are ignored.
+
+The result is printed on *standard out* as JSON: a string, or ``null``
+if none of the versions is a non-prerelease version::
+
+    $ pysemver latest 1.10.0 2.0.0-rc.1 1.2.0
+    "1.10.0"
+    $ pysemver latest 2.0.0-rc.1
+    null
+
+If any version is not a valid version, nothing is printed on standard
+out and the command fails with return code 2.
+
+
 Return Code
 -----------
 
